PL/SQL Exception Handling  
An error occurs during the program execution is called Exception in PL/SQL.  
PL/SQL facilitates programmers to catch such conditions using exception block in the  
program and an appropriate action is taken against the error condition.  
Syyntax:  
EXCEPTION  
<exception handling goes here >  
WHEN exception1 THEN  
exception1-handling-statements  
........  
WHEN others THEN  
exception3-handling-statements  
END;  
Example:  
In EXECPTION,  
EXCEPTION  
WHEN no_data_found THEN  
dbms_output.put_line('No such customer!');  
WHEN others THEN  
dbms_output.put_line('Error!'); 
NO_DATA_FOUND is a pre-defined exception which is raised when a SELECT INTO  
statement returns no rows.  
If a value is return from table then normal program will be execute and work as per the  
code, but if any error occurred during execution suppose value is not return from table  
so the program raises the run-time exception NO_DATA_FOUND, which is captured in  
EXCEPTION block.  
